    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '---'; cat -A process_data.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '---'; cat -A generate_report.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've identified all the issues:\n\n1. **run_pipeline.sh**: Correct shebang and Unix line endings (good), but lacks execute permission (rw-r--r--). Needs chmod +x.\n2. **collect_data.sh**: Has permission `--wx--x--x` — no READ permission for owner. A script's interpreter (bash) needs to read the file, so it must be readable. Needs read permission added.\n3. **process_data.sh**: Has Windows-style line endings (^M$ = \\r\\n) — the classic hint issue. The shebang is `#!/bin/bash^M` which is `bash\\r`. Needs CRLF removed AND execute permission (rw-r--r--).\n4. **generate_report.sh**: Bad shebang `#!/bin/nonexistent` which doesn't exist. Needs to be fixed to `#!/bin/bash`.\n\nLet me fix all of these.",
  "plan": "1. Fix process_data.sh CRLF endings with sed, then add execute permission.\n2. Fix generate_report.sh shebang to /bin/bash.\n3. Add execute permission to run_pipeline.sh.\n4. Add read permission to collect_data.sh.\n5. Run the pipeline to verify it works.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's/\\r$//' process_data.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i 's|^#!/bin/nonexistent|#!/bin/bash|' generate_report.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "chmod +x run_pipeline.sh process_data.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "chmod u+r collect_data.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat -A process_data.sh | head -3\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -1 generate_report.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "All fixes applied successfully:\n- process_data.sh: CRLF removed (now clean `\\n` endings)\n- generate_report.sh: shebang fixed to `#!/bin/bash`\n- run_pipeline.sh: now executable (rwxr-xr-x)\n- process_data.sh: now executable\n- collect_data.sh: now has read permission for owner (rwx--x--x)\n\nNow I'll run the pipeline to verify it executes successfully.",
  "plan": "Execute ./run_pipeline.sh and check the output and exit code. Then verify the output files were created in /data/output.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "./run_pipeline.sh\n",
